From: ShellOS <161210761+sahil-mpatki@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/poc: fix out-of-bounds read and UB shift in poc_cpumask_to_u64

The unaligned slow path always read the cpumask word after base_word and
shifted it left by (64 - shift). With shift == 0 that is a shift by 64
(undefined; on x86 the count wraps so the extra word is ORed into the
result), and with NR_CPUS <= 64 the extra word lies past the end of the
cpumask. UBSAN reports both at boot from select_task_rq_fair() while
sched_poc_aligned is not yet enabled.

Return the low word when there is nothing to shift, and treat a missing
next word as empty.
---
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.h
@@ -3246,7 +3246,17 @@
 		/* Slow path: shift required (e.g., Threadripper) */
 		int shift = sd_share->poc_affinity_shift;
 		u64 lo = cpumask_bits(mask)[base_word];
-		u64 hi = cpumask_bits(mask)[base_word + 1];
+		u64 hi;
+
+		/*
+		 * shift == 0 would make "hi << 64" undefined (x86 wraps it to
+		 * a no-op and ORs @hi in), and with NR_CPUS <= 64 there is no
+		 * second word to read at all.
+		 */
+		if (!shift)
+			return lo;
+		hi = base_word + 1 < BITS_TO_LONGS(NR_CPUS) ?
+			cpumask_bits(mask)[base_word + 1] : 0;
 		return (lo >> shift) | (hi << (64 - shift));
 	}
 }
